---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
import { SITE } from "../config/site.mjs";

const title = "Privacy — Your Voice Never Leaves Your Device | Veena";
const description =
	"Veena's privacy policy in plain words: no account, no cloud, no telemetry, no data collection. Transcription runs on your device and recordings stay on it.";

const canonical = `${SITE.url}/privacy/`;
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} canonicalURL={canonical}>
	<Header />
	<main id="main-content" role="main">
		<section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-16 md:py-20">
			<h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8">
				What Veena does and does not do with your voice
			</h1>

			<div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-gray-700">
				<p class="text-xl">
					Veena exists because dictation tools that upload your audio are a bad
					fit for real life. This page explains, in plain words, what happens to
					your data. The short version: it stays with you.
				</p>

				<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900">
					What leaves your device
				</h2>
				<p>
					Almost nothing. When you set the app up for the first time, Veena
					downloads a speech model from our servers. That download contains no
					personal data; it is a fixed file, the same for everyone, and it
					happens once per model. After that, transcription needs no network at
					all.
				</p>

				<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900">
					What stays on your device
				</h2>
				<p>
					Everything else. Your recordings and transcripts are stored in the
					app's local database on your phone or computer. Nothing is synced,
					backed up to our servers, or shared. Delete an entry in the history
					and it is gone.
				</p>

				<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900">What we do not have</h2>
				<ul>
					<li>No account. There is nothing to sign up for.</li>
					<li>No analytics or telemetry in the apps.</li>
					<li>No ads and no third-party trackers.</li>
					<li>
						No audio uploads. The recognition engine runs locally, so the audio
						never has to leave the device for transcription.
					</li>
				</ul>

				<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900">Permissions</h2>
				<p>
					The mobile apps ask for microphone access, because recording your
					voice is the job. On Android the app also holds the network
					permission, which it uses only to fetch the speech model on first
					setup. The Windows app uses the microphone for recording and can paste
					your transcript into another application.
				</p>

				<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900">The app stores</h2>
				<p>
					Google Play and the App Store handle their own installation and
					payment data under their own policies; Veena never sees it. Veena
					itself collects no data, which matches the "no data collected"
					declaration in its Play Store and App Store listings.
				</p>

				<h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900">Questions</h2>
				<p>
					Write to
					<a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`} class="text-blue-600 hover:underline"
						>{SITE.email}</a
					> and a human answers.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>
	<Footer />
</Layout>
